            <div xml:id="d818">

                <pb facs="0880" n="868" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg868"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.61/164: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-08T19:00:00+03:00">January 8, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 8—3:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. My telegram 30, January 8, 6 p.m. I have had a further talk with Lozovzki
                    this evening with respect to the difficulties which the Embassy has been
                    encountering and which have not as yet been disposed of. He assured me that he
                    would give these matters his personal attention in the course of the next few
                    days and would endeavor to dispose of them to my satisfaction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
